body:
Upvote for this issue. This just hit me. My testcase:
```python
from abc import ABCMeta, abstractmethod
from typing import TypeVar, Generic, Callable

A = TypeVar("A")
B = TypeVar("B")

class Functor(Generic[A], metaclass=ABCMeta):
    @abstractmethod
    def map(self, f: Callable[[A], B]) -> "Functor[B]":
        ...

def fmap(container: "Functor[A]", func: Callable[[A], B]) -> "Functor[B]":
    return container.map(func)
```
for which mypy gives me:
```
example.py:13: error: Argument 1 to "map" of "Functor" has incompatible type "Callable[[A], B]"; expected "Callable[[B], B]"
```
